    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0576" n="506" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg506"/>

                <head>No. 298.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-16"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 16,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous correspondence
                    concerning the raids of Canadian Indians into the northwestern Territories of
                    this country, I have the honor to inclose herewith for your information copies
                    of correspondence which I have received from my colleague, the Secretary of War,
                    in relation to the disposition made of certain Cree Indians held as prisoners at
                    Fort Assinniboine.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>




